---
import { type ui } from '../i18n/ui';

interface Props {
  lang: keyof typeof ui;
}

const { lang } = Astro.props;

const personalImageAlt = "Álvaro Escobar";
---

<article class="flex flex-col items-center justify-center gap-8 text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 md:flex-row">
  <div class="[&>p]:mb-4 [&>p>strong]:text-violet-500 dark:[&>p>strong]:text-violet-400 [&>p>strong]:font-normal [&>p>strong]:font-mono text-pretty order-2 md:order-1">
    {
      lang === 'es' ? (
        <p>
          Me llamo Álvaro pero en internet me conocen como l3onkers. Empecé en el mundo del desarrollo automatizando pequeños scripts para servidores y, hoy en día, diseño <strong>arquitecturas escalables Serverless para millones de usuarios</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          A lo largo de mi carrera, he colaborado en la migración de infraestructuras críticas hacia la nube y he liderado la adopción de <strong>metodologías GitOps y contenedores en Kubernetes</strong>. Mi objetivo siempre ha sido asegurar la alta disponibilidad.
        </p>
        <p>
          Actualmente, me encuentro profundizando en patrones avanzados de despliegue continuo y <strong>creando herramientas open-source</strong> para facilitar la observabilidad en ecosistemas distribuidos.
        </p>
      ) : (
        <p>
          My name is Álvaro, but on the internet I'm known as l3onkers. I started in the development world by automating small scripts for servers and, today, I design <strong>scalable Serverless architectures for millions of users</strong>.
        </p>
        <p>
          Throughout my career, I have collaborated in the migration of critical infrastructures to the cloud and led the adoption of <strong>GitOps methodologies and containers in Kubernetes</strong>. My goal has always been to ensure high availability.
        </p>
        <p>
          Currently, I'm deepening my knowledge in advanced continuous deployment patterns and <strong>creating open-source tools</strong> to facilitate observability in distributed ecosystems.
        </p>
      )
    }
  </div>

  <img width="200" height="200" src="/favicon.png" alt={personalImageAlt} class="order-1 object-cover w-64 h-full p-1 md:order-2 rotate-3 lg:p-2 lg:w-64 aspect-square rounded-2xl bg-black/20 dark:bg-yellow-500/5 ring-1 ring-black/70 dark:ring-white/20" style="object-position: 50% 50%">
</article>
